      "problem": "Simplify the expression $|-5x|-2\\cdot |-2x|.$",
      "worked_solution": "Firstly, since $|-a|=|a|,$ we can write our expression as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|5x|-2\\cdot |2x|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we distribute the absolute value over the multiplication, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|5x|-2\\cdot |2x| & = \\\\ |5|\\cdot |x|-2\\cdot |2|\\cdot |x| & = \\\\ 5|x|-2\\cdot 2\\cdot |x| & = \\\\ 5|x|-4|x| & = \\\\ |x| & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
